@startuml UC-L1-view-the-audit-trail-design-sequence
!include ../../domain/diagrams/_style.puml
hide footbox
skinparam maxMessageSize 50
title UC-L1 View the audit trail (design sequence)
' Design level (decision 9), drawn against docs/domain/diagrams/audit-design.puml. Analysis: UC-L1-view-the-audit-trail-analysis-sequence.puml.
' Step numbers are the main flow numbers of UC-L1.
' BUILT today, inside Access: GET /audit, the administrator guard, SqlAudit.entries() and the admin accounts page. Account entries only.
' PLANNED (decision 14): the Audit context, AuditService.read(caller), AuditRepository, the Caller, kind and details columns,
' names and emails at the time, and project entries. The lower part shows how entries arrive (AC-29, AC-30), a flow of UC-A4, UC-P1 and UC-P2.
' Decisions 21 and 22, ADR 0011: one API database session for each request, shared by the change and its entry; the API role has INSERT and SELECT only;
' the database sets the time; reading and every refusal write a security log line (decision 17) and no audit entry.
' Not drawn: the token check (UC-A1 step 9) and the web page.

actor "Administrator" as AD
participant "Routes\n(API)" as R #E6F0FB
participant "Audit-\nService\n(planned)" as S #E7F4EA
participant "Audit-\nRepository\n(SqlAuditEntries)" as AR #EEE7F7
participant "Security\nlog" as SL #EEE7F7
participant "Access or\nProjects\nservice" as OS #E7F4EA
participant "AuditLog\n(own port)" as AL #EEE7F7
participant "Bridge\n(composition/)" as BR #EEE7F7

AD -> R : 1 GET /audit
R -> R : 2 guard: token, account found, active, administrator, so a Caller (Audit's own)
alt no token, or not an administrator
  R -> SL : 6 log line: refused (401 no token, 403 others)
  R --> AD : 2 401 or 403, no entry
else
  R -> S : 2 read(caller)
  S -> AR : 3 list_newest_first() (same session as the request)
  AR --> S : 3 entries of both kinds
  S -> SL : 6 log line: the trail was read
  S --> R : entries
  R --> AD : 4, 5 200 the entries, with kind, details and the names at the time
end

== How the entries got there (other flows: AC-29 and AC-30 are UC-P1 and UC-P2; AC-77 is UC-A4) ==
OS -> AL : record(actor, action, target, people, names and emails, reason)
AL -> BR : the same call, in the context's own words
BR -> S : record(entry), the Caller translated here
S -> AR : add(entry), on the same session as the change (the database sets the time)
note over AR
  The API role may INSERT and SELECT only.
  A repeated deactivation or a Keycloak failure
  adds another entry, never an edit.
end note
@enduml
